  "description": "The EXACT-MULTIPLE-OF-TEN boundary reached by PF8, and the deliberate counterpart of case04: case04's fill loop ends EARLY on end-of-file and its page number comes from :317-318, whereas this case COMPLETES the ten-row page and its page number comes from :306-307. Twenty records on file and an anchor of 0000000000000010 carried in CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-LAST, so :285 - an abbreviated combined relation reading 'NOT = DFHENTER AND DFHPF7 AND DFHPF3' - is TRUE for PF8 and the skip READNEXT at :286 consumes record ten before the page begins at record eleven. The loop at :297 then paints records eleven to twenty into ALL TEN slots and ends on its own bound with WS-IDX at eleven, not on end-of-file, so at :305 TRANSACT-EOF is still false and WS-ERR-FLG is still off: :306-307 computes 1 + 1 = 2. Only THEN does the look-ahead READNEXT at :308 reach DFHRESP(ENDFILE) at :639, because record twenty was the last - and that arm sets TRANSACT-EOF, moves 'You have reached the bottom of the page...' at :642 into WS-MESSAGE, moves -1 into TRNIDINL and performs SEND-TRNLST-SCREEN at :645, but it does NOT set WS-ERR-FLG. The IF at :309 is therefore false and :312 SETs NEXT-PAGE-NO, which is the counterintuitive outcome this case exists to pin: a FULL ten-row page that reports CDEMO-CT00-NEXT-PAGE-FLG as N. It is the mirror of case14, which shares this anchor and this page number but finds record twenty-one and so takes :310 instead. Because slot ten IS reached, :439 writes CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-LAST as well as :393 writing CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-FIRST. Two sends, in order: the ENDFILE arm's at :645 and the tail at :326, and WS-MESSAGE is not cleared between them, so the same 80-byte text is painted twice. The page size of ten is behaviour rather than configuration and this case is its clearest proof - a page size of nine or eleven would move the boundary and change the page number, the next-page flag and the send count together. Note that COTRN00C LISTS transactions; the class is named TransactionMenuController because the mandated name is honoured verbatim while the behaviour is taken from the source. PROVENANCE: statically derived by reading app/cbl/COTRN00C.cbl:257-328, :381-445 and :624-653 against app/cpy/CVTRA05Y.cpy, app/cpy-bms/COTRN00.CPY and app/cpy/COCOM01Y.cpy. It was never captured from a live COBOL run - no runtime here can execute these programs - so every value above traces to a source line rather than to an observation.",
